{"id":"demand-and-supply","title":"Economics: demand and supply","subject":"Economics","label":"JAMB · WAEC","exams":["jamb","waec"],"language":"en","seconds":189,"duration":188.96,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":482,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"Market puzzle","start":0,"end":18.795},{"id":"explain","title":"Demand","start":18.795,"end":42.015},{"id":"explain2","title":"Supply and equilibrium","start":42.015,"end":92.605},{"id":"example","title":"Tomato market","start":92.605,"end":124.725},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":124.725,"end":135.465},{"id":"answer","title":"Answer","start":135.465,"end":146.405},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Common mistakes","start":146.405,"end":168.255},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap","start":168.255,"end":188.96}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":4.89,"text":"I'm Kora. Have you ever reached the market and found tomatoes suddenly expensive?","w":[0.62,0.8,1.64,1.78,2.02,2.24,2.5,2.62,3.06,3.22,3.48,3.96,4.36]},{"s":0,"a":5.34,"b":8.84,"text":"Nothing changed in your need for tomatoes, yet the price moved.","w":[5.5,5.9,6.3,6.38,6.54,6.76,6.9,7.78,7.96,8.08,8.42]},{"s":0,"a":9.14,"b":14.91,"text":"Today we explain why, using demand and supply. This is the heart of JAMB and WAEC Economics.","w":[9.18,9.58,9.72,10.14,10.82,11.1,11.56,11.68,12.52,12.74,12.86,12.98,13.18,13.3,13.7,13.82,14.26]},{"s":0,"a":15.21,"b":18.37,"text":"By the end, you will read any market like an economist.","w":[15.24,15.44,15.64,16.14,16.28,16.48,16.88,17.08,17.48,17.66,17.76]},{"s":1,"a":19.22,"b":24.59,"text":"Demand is the quantity of a good consumers are willing and able to buy at each price in a given period.","w":[19.24,19.68,19.8,19.94,20.46,20.56,20.64,20.86,21.5,21.66,22.1,22.34,22.58,22.74,23.12,23.26,23.5,23.82,23.9,23.98,24.22]},{"s":1,"a":24.89,"b":30.59,"text":"The law of demand says that, other things being equal, a higher price lowers the quantity demanded.","w":[24.92,25.08,25.38,25.48,25.94,26.22,26.9,27.14,27.42,27.72,28.36,28.46,28.8,29.16,29.52,29.64,30.1]},{"s":1,"a":30.89,"b":33.37,"text":"Economists call that ceteris paribus.","w":[30.96,31.66,31.9,32.22,32.7]},{"s":1,"a":33.67,"b":37.75,"text":"Think of Ada buying garri. If garri becomes costly, she buys less.","w":[33.68,33.92,34.14,34.42,34.74,35.64,35.78,36.06,36.42,36.94,37.1,37.38]},{"s":1,"a":38.05,"b":41.59,"text":"So the demand curve slopes downward from left to right.","w":[38.14,38.3,38.44,38.94,39.36,39.84,40.4,40.62,41.04,41.2]},{"s":2,"a":42.44,"b":47.1,"text":"Supply is the quantity producers are willing and able to offer for sale at each price.","w":[42.52,43.1,43.22,43.36,43.8,44.4,44.54,44.92,45.08,45.3,45.48,45.74,45.9,46.3,46.46,46.64]},{"s":2,"a":47.4,"b":53.17,"text":"The law of supply says a higher price raises the quantity supplied, so the supply curve slopes upward.","w":[47.4,47.56,47.86,48,48.52,48.82,48.92,49.26,49.6,49.94,50.06,50.46,51.24,51.38,51.54,51.98,52.34,52.82]},{"s":2,"a":53.47,"b":59.41,"text":"Equilibrium is where quantity demanded equals quantity supplied, giving the equilibrium price and quantity.","w":[53.52,54.16,54.26,54.5,55.02,55.64,56,56.48,57.36,57.6,57.74,58.28,58.72,58.88]},{"s":2,"a":59.71,"b":64.21,"text":"Above equilibrium there is excess supply, a surplus, so price falls.","w":[59.8,60.26,60.88,61.1,61.38,61.78,62.36,62.48,63.22,63.44,63.76]},{"s":2,"a":64.51,"b":69.31,"text":"Below equilibrium there is excess demand, a shortage, so price rises.","w":[64.54,64.94,65.6,65.8,66,66.38,67.22,67.34,68.22,68.42,68.78]},{"s":2,"a":69.61,"b":74.64,"text":"A change in the good's own price moves you along the curve: a change in quantity demanded.","w":[69.7,69.82,70.26,70.34,70.48,70.88,71.08,71.52,71.8,71.96,72.22,72.34,73.12,73.22,73.56,73.7,74.16]},{"s":2,"a":74.94,"b":78.86,"text":"A change in another factor shifts the whole curve: a change in demand.","w":[75.02,75.12,75.5,75.62,75.98,76.44,76.74,76.84,77.06,77.92,78.02,78.34,78.44]},{"s":2,"a":79.16,"b":86.09,"text":"For demand, factors include income, tastes, substitute and complement prices, population and expectations.","w":[79.2,79.36,80.16,80.62,81.06,81.68,82.44,83.08,83.24,83.7,84.4,85.12,85.26]},{"s":2,"a":86.39,"b":92.18,"text":"For supply, factors include production cost, technology, weather, taxes and subsidies.","w":[86.44,86.6,87.38,87.82,88.24,88.66,89.28,90.26,90.9,91.44,91.58]},{"s":3,"a":93.03,"b":95.78,"text":"Imagine a poor tomato harvest in Nigeria.","w":[93.12,93.66,93.76,94.06,94.52,95.08,95.18]},{"s":3,"a":96.08,"b":101.65,"text":"At every price, farmers can now offer fewer tomatoes, so supply shifts to the left.","w":[96.16,96.38,96.64,97.44,97.9,98.1,98.44,98.8,99.08,100.06,100.24,100.68,101.06,101.18,101.3]},{"s":3,"a":101.95,"b":108.11,"text":"Say tomatoes sold for two hundred naira before. After the poor harvest, they may sell for four hundred.","w":[102.04,102.3,102.82,103.1,103.28,103.54,103.88,104.24,105.3,105.52,105.64,105.88,106.68,106.86,107.04,107.34,107.54,107.78]},{"s":3,"a":108.41,"b":113.97,"text":"At the old price, buyers want more tomatoes than farmers have, creating excess demand.","w":[108.48,108.56,108.76,108.94,109.92,110.36,110.6,110.84,111.32,111.52,111.92,112.6,113.14,113.52]},{"s":3,"a":114.27,"b":118.96,"text":"The price rises until quantity demanded equals the new lower quantity supplied.","w":[114.3,114.44,114.84,115.4,115.72,116.2,116.82,117.22,117.38,117.66,118,118.46]},{"s":3,"a":119.26,"b":124.3,"text":"So the equilibrium price of tomatoes rises, and the equilibrium quantity falls.","w":[119.34,119.52,119.72,120.4,120.74,120.86,121.34,122.36,122.48,122.68,123.34,123.82]},{"s":4,"a":125.15,"b":132.35,"text":"The price of rice rises, so people buy more beans. Has demand for beans shifted, or is it a movement along the curve?","w":[125.18,125.32,125.7,125.82,126.12,126.88,127.08,127.4,127.62,127.86,128.8,129.02,129.38,129.54,129.86,130.72,130.9,131.04,131.12,131.22,131.66,131.92,132.04]},{"s":4,"a":132.8,"b":135.04,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[132.8,133.12,133.46,133.6,133.9,134.54,134.7]},{"s":5,"a":135.89,"b":143.46,"text":"It is a shift to the right. Rice and beans are substitutes, so a higher rice price increases demand for beans at every price.","w":[135.96,136.08,136.2,136.3,136.66,136.78,136.92,137.72,138.16,138.3,138.7,138.84,139.86,140.06,140.16,140.56,140.86,141.26,141.78,142.12,142.26,142.62,142.8,143.02]},{"s":5,"a":143.76,"b":145.98,"text":"Nothing about beans themselves changed.","w":[143.94,144.3,144.56,144.9,145.46]},{"s":6,"a":146.83,"b":151.2,"text":"First, do not confuse a change in demand with a change in quantity demanded.","w":[146.9,147.4,147.56,147.76,148.26,148.36,148.7,148.8,149.4,149.58,149.68,150.02,150.16,150.7]},{"s":6,"a":151.5,"b":155.57,"text":"Own price moves you along the curve; other factors shift the curve.","w":[151.62,151.84,152.24,152.52,152.68,152.94,153.08,154.08,154.3,154.84,155.12,155.24]},{"s":6,"a":155.87,"b":159.92,"text":"Second, draw demand downward and supply upward from left to right.","w":[155.98,156.7,156.96,157.3,158.08,158.22,158.7,159.02,159.22,159.46,159.6]},{"s":6,"a":160.22,"b":165.33,"text":"Third, remember demand and supply require willingness and ability, not just desire.","w":[160.3,161.04,161.48,162.02,162.14,162.62,163.08,163.66,163.76,164.46,164.68,164.9]},{"s":6,"a":165.63,"b":167.83,"text":"So always check the cause before you draw.","w":[165.7,166,166.32,166.58,166.7,167.06,167.36,167.5]},{"s":7,"a":168.68,"b":171.59,"text":"Demand slopes downward; supply slopes upward.","w":[168.72,169.16,169.56,170.3,170.78,171.28]},{"s":7,"a":171.89,"b":175.52,"text":"Equilibrium is where quantity demanded equals quantity supplied.","w":[171.96,172.62,172.72,173.02,173.52,174.14,174.48,175]},{"s":7,"a":175.82,"b":179.13,"text":"Own price moves along the curve; other factors shift it.","w":[175.9,176.14,176.52,176.82,177.06,177.18,178.08,178.3,178.74,179.04]},{"s":7,"a":179.43,"b":184.4,"text":"Exam tip: name the cause first, then decide between movement and shift.","w":[179.54,179.94,180.66,180.94,181.04,181.44,182.26,182.46,182.96,183.34,183.86,184]},{"s":7,"a":184.7,"b":188.36,"text":"Keep practising with Knowzone, and you will master demand and supply.","w":[184.74,185,185.52,185.7,186.4,186.52,186.64,186.84,187.26,187.78,187.92]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"Market puzzle","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Tomatoes suddenly expensive?"},{"at":5.24,"kind":"text","text":"Need unchanged, price moved"},{"at":9.04,"kind":"text","text":"Demand & supply explain why"},{"at":15.11,"kind":"text","text":"Read any market like an economist"}]},{"at":18.97,"heading":"Demand","items":[{"at":19.12,"kind":"term","text":"Demand","detail":"Quantity consumers are willing and able to buy at each price"},{"at":24.79,"kind":"term","text":"Law of demand","detail":"Higher price lowers quantity demanded, other things equal"},{"at":30.79,"kind":"term","text":"Ceteris paribus","detail":"Other things being equal"},{"at":33.57,"kind":"text","text":"Ada: costly garri → she buys less"},{"at":37.95,"kind":"text","text":"Demand curve slopes downward from left to right"}]},{"at":42.19,"heading":"Supply & equilibrium","items":[{"at":42.34,"kind":"term","text":"Supply","detail":"Quantity producers are willing and able to offer at each price"},{"at":47.3,"kind":"term","text":"Law of supply","detail":"Higher price raises quantity supplied; curve slopes upward"},{"at":53.37,"kind":"term","text":"Equilibrium","detail":"Quantity demanded = quantity supplied; sets price and quantity"},{"at":53.37,"kind":"image","text":"Equilibrium: where demand and supply cross","src":"curves.webp","credit":"SilverStar at English Wikipedia · Public domain · Wikimedia Commons"},{"at":59.61,"kind":"text","text":"Above equilibrium: surplus → price falls"},{"at":64.41,"kind":"text","text":"Below equilibrium: shortage → price rises"}]},{"at":69.36,"heading":"Movement vs shift","items":[{"at":69.51,"kind":"text","text":"Own price → movement along curve"},{"at":74.84,"kind":"text","text":"Other factors → shift whole curve"},{"at":79.06,"kind":"term","text":"Demand shifters","detail":"Income, tastes, substitute/complement prices, population, expectations"},{"at":86.29,"kind":"term","text":"Supply shifters","detail":"Production cost, technology, weather, taxes, subsidies"}]},{"at":92.78,"heading":"Tomato market","items":[{"at":92.93,"kind":"text","text":"Poor tomato harvest in Nigeria"},{"at":95.98,"kind":"text","text":"At every price, farmers offer fewer → supply shifts left"},{"at":101.85,"kind":"formula","text":"P: ₦200 → ₦400"},{"at":108.31,"kind":"text","text":"At old price: excess demand (shortage)"}]},{"at":114.02,"heading":"New equilibrium","items":[{"at":114.17,"kind":"text","text":"Price rises until Qd = new lower Qs"},{"at":119.16,"kind":"text","text":"Equilibrium price ↑, equilibrium quantity ↓"}]},{"at":124.72,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":124.72,"kind":"question","text":"The price of rice rises, so people buy more beans. Has demand for beans shifted, or is it a movement along the curve?"}]},{"at":135.64,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":135.79,"kind":"text","text":"Shift right: rice & beans are substitutes"},{"at":143.66,"kind":"text","text":"Nothing about beans changed"}]},{"at":146.58,"heading":"Common mistakes","items":[{"at":146.73,"kind":"wrong","text":"Change in demand = change in quantity demanded"},{"at":155.77,"kind":"wrong","text":"Demand and supply drawn sloping the wrong way"},{"at":165.53,"kind":"tip","text":"Check the cause first, then draw"}]},{"at":168.43,"heading":"Recap","items":[{"at":168.58,"kind":"text","text":"Demand slopes down; supply slopes up"},{"at":171.79,"kind":"text","text":"Equilibrium: Qd = Qs"},{"at":175.72,"kind":"text","text":"Own price → along; other factors → shift"},{"at":179.33,"kind":"tip","text":"Name cause first, then movement or shift"},{"at":184.6,"kind":"text","text":"Keep practising with Knowzone"}]}],"check":{"at":135.29,"seconds":10,"question":"The price of rice rises, so people buy more beans. Has demand for beans shifted, or is it a movement along the curve?","answer":"Shift right: rice and beans are substitutes; higher rice price raises demand for beans at every price."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[{"title":"Supply-demand-equilibrium.svg","author":"SilverStar at English Wikipedia","licence":"Public domain","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Supply-demand-equilibrium.svg"}],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}